1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:05,613
AI Moderator lets you design a live
discussion around your learning goals.

2
00:00:05,746 --> 00:00:10,006
You shape the activity and
choose how AI supports it.

3
00:00:10,082 --> 00:00:14,514
Select a shared moderation profile
prepared by your administrator.

4
00:00:14,647 --> 00:00:18,861
This sets the moderator’s
approach, instructions and timing.

5
00:00:18,938 --> 00:00:21,924
Give the dialogue a topic and a clear task.

6
00:00:22,057 --> 00:00:27,074
Here, students compare nuclear power
within a low-carbon electricity system.

7
00:00:27,151 --> 00:00:29,071
Set the start and end times.

8
00:00:29,124 --> 00:00:32,168
Choose the number of participants and groups.

9
00:00:32,244 --> 00:00:35,403
Share an individual join code with each student.

10
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:38,316
Each code connects them to their group.

11
00:00:38,393 --> 00:00:42,641
During the activity, view its
status, groups and dialogue details.

12
00:00:42,774 --> 00:00:44,786
You can end the dialogue when needed.

13
00:00:44,863 --> 00:00:48,722
The moderator participates
according to the selected profile.

14
00:00:48,911 --> 00:00:52,586
Students can also request help
in the shared conversation.

15
00:00:52,663 --> 00:00:54,974
You set the educational context.

16
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:58,460
Students examine evidence and
develop their conclusions.
